{"name":"Cheese Please","hex":"#ff9613","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheese","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dairy product made from curdled or cultured milk.","Any particular variety of cheese."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare curds for making cheese.","To make holes in a pattern of circuitry to decrease pattern density."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheese"},{"term":"please","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.","To desire; to will; to be pleased by."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Used to make a polite request."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/please"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese","wikidata":"Q10943"},{"title":"Please","blocks":[{"text":"Please is a word used in the English language to indicate politeness and respect while making a request. Derived from shortening the phrase \"if you please\" or \"if it please(s) you\", the term has taken on substantial nuance based on its intonation and the relationship between the persons between whom it is used. In much of the Western world, use of the word is considered proper etiquette, and parents and authority figures often imprint upon children the importance of saying \"please\" when asking for something from an early age, leading to the description of the term as \"the magic word\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg/330px-Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Please","wikidata":"Q26175857"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/500px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/1280px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/500px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cheeses in art: Still Life with Cheeses, Almonds and Pretzels, Clara Peeters, c. 1615","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/9-alimenti%2C_formaggi%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casanatense_4182..jpg/500px-9-alimenti%2C_formaggi%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casanatense_4182..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/9-alimenti%2C_formaggi%2CTaccuino_San